+Measure OCI-to-ext4 conversion IO before selecting optimizations. Adds observe-only counters and histograms with fixed labels, preserves conversion/cache/singleflight behavior, and keeps ociconv changes localized to instrumentation calls. Existing filecache metrics are aggregate across all artifacts: FastLinkFile records hit/miss, but ContainsFile does not. Existing workspace write operations include directory-to-image mke2fs calls but lack reads, phase distributions, and OCI isolation. Existing image-fetch latency includes the outer per-image pull mutex wait and registry/authentication work, so it answers total task image-fetch wait but cannot count actual ext4 conversions.
+
+Optional measurement flags (all default off):
+
+- `executor.ext4_conversion_track_keys`: 4096-key LRU of successful conversions plus at most 4096 active flight hashes. Tracks cache-miss reconversion attempts and overlapping flights without retaining credentials. A recently successful key missing from filecache is evidence of eviction/removal, not proof of eviction. Restart, history eviction, and active overflow undercount; simultaneous first conversions are not classified as reconversions.
+- `executor.ext4_conversion_sample_process_io`: adds two `/proc/self/io` reads per measured scope (cleanup has two scopes). These physical IO deltas include concurrent executor work and potentially reaped children; do not sum process and child sources. Child rusage is physical IO in 512-byte units, not logical bytes copied; cached reads may be zero. Process-only phases have no IO samples while this flag is disabled. Missing observations are omitted rather than reported as zero.
+- `executor.ext4_conversion_sample_image_size`: adds one stat per successful generated image for apparent and allocated sizes.
+
+Lookup counters count operations, not unique pulls; contains includes singleflight cache rechecks. Conversion counts are attempts after that recheck. Deduped waiter counts exclude canceled callers and the executing caller (the shared return value alone also counts the leader). Credential overlap counts each starting conversion which overlaps another flight for the same storage/image key. Each conversion emits exactly one duration sample for each of the five phases. Cleanup sums unpack-directory and temporary-image removal; repeated scopes are aggregated before flushing. Failed operations are included, and unreached phases emit zero duration. Available IO is likewise aggregated into one sample per phase/source/direction; unavailable IO is omitted. The conversion wait stage includes cache recheck, conversion, singleflight wait, and final link; existing pull timing includes authentication and other pull work. Scrape target `instance` identifies the executor, without adding an executor label.
+
+| Metric | Question answered | Type and labels | New/existing | Example PromQL |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `buildbuddy_remote_execution_ext4_image_conversions` | How many conversion attempts per executor? | Counter, none | New | `sum by (instance) (increase(buildbuddy_remote_execution_ext4_image_conversions[1h]))` |
+| `buildbuddy_remote_execution_ext4_image_cache_lookups` | How often do contains/link lookups hit? | Counter, method=contains/link; status=hit/miss/error (link failures are misses) | New | `sum by (instance, method, status) (rate(buildbuddy_remote_execution_ext4_image_cache_lookups[5m]))` |
+| `buildbuddy_remote_execution_ext4_image_reconversions` | How often is a recently converted filecache key converted after a miss? | Counter, recent=true/false; opt-in | New | `sum by (instance) (increase(buildbuddy_remote_execution_ext4_image_reconversions{recent="true"}[1h]))` |
+| `buildbuddy_remote_execution_ext4_image_credential_overlap` | How often do different credentials cause concurrent conversions of the same image? | Counter, tracking=bounded; opt-in | New | `sum by (instance) (increase(buildbuddy_remote_execution_ext4_image_credential_overlap[1h]))` |
+| `buildbuddy_remote_execution_ext4_image_deduped_waiters` | How many completed callers did singleflight dedupe? | Counter, none | New | `sum by (instance) (increase(buildbuddy_remote_execution_ext4_image_deduped_waiters[1h]))` |
+| `buildbuddy_remote_execution_ext4_image_phase_duration_usec` | Which phases take time? | Histogram, phase=extract/size/mke2fs/filecache_add/cleanup | New | `histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (phase, le) (rate(buildbuddy_remote_execution_ext4_image_phase_duration_usec_bucket[1h])))` |
+| `buildbuddy_remote_execution_ext4_image_phase_io_bytes` | What physical read/write IO occurs per phase? | Histogram, phase; source=child_rusage/process; direction=read/write | New | `sum by (phase, source, direction) (rate(buildbuddy_remote_execution_ext4_image_phase_io_bytes_sum[1h])) / sum by (phase, source, direction) (rate(buildbuddy_remote_execution_ext4_image_phase_io_bytes_count[1h]))` |
+| `buildbuddy_remote_execution_ext4_image_size_bytes` | How large/sparse are generated images? | Histogram, kind=apparent/allocated; opt-in | New | `histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (kind, le) (rate(buildbuddy_remote_execution_ext4_image_size_bytes_bucket[1h])))` |
+| `buildbuddy_remote_execution_ext4_mke2fs_version` | Which e2fsprogs version is installed? | Info gauge, version | New | `count by (version) (buildbuddy_remote_execution_ext4_mke2fs_version == 1)` |
+| `buildbuddy_firecracker_stage_duration_usec` | How long do tasks wait for image conversion within pull/init? | Histogram, stage; reuse pull_image, add image_conversion | Existing, new stage | `histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (stage, le) (rate(buildbuddy_firecracker_stage_duration_usec_bucket{stage=~"pull_image\|image_conversion"}[1h])))` |
+| `buildbuddy_remote_execution_file_cache_requests` | What is overall executor filecache hit/miss pressure? | Counter, status | Existing | `sum by (instance, status) (rate(buildbuddy_remote_execution_file_cache_requests[5m]))` |
+| `buildbuddy_remote_execution_file_cache_op_latency_usec` | How slow are filecache operations across artifacts? | Histogram, op | Existing | `histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (op, le) (rate(buildbuddy_remote_execution_file_cache_op_latency_usec_bucket[1h])))` |
+| `buildbuddy_remote_execution_file_cache_last_eviction_age_usec` | Are entries evicted soon after being added? | Gauge, none | Existing | `buildbuddy_remote_execution_file_cache_last_eviction_age_usec / 1e6` |
+| `buildbuddy_remote_execution_file_cache_added_file_size_bytes` | What sizes enter filecache overall? | Histogram, none | Existing | `histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(buildbuddy_remote_execution_file_cache_added_file_size_bytes_bucket[1h])))` |
+| `buildbuddy_remote_execution_file_cache_added_file_bytes_count` | How many bytes of artifacts are admitted (not physical IO)? | Counter, group_id (pre-existing label only) | Existing | `sum by (instance) (rate(buildbuddy_remote_execution_file_cache_added_file_bytes_count[5m]))` |
+| `buildbuddy_firecracker_workspace_conversion_disk_write_ops` | What mke2fs/debugfs write operations are already recorded? | Counter, command | Existing | `sum by (command) (rate(buildbuddy_firecracker_workspace_conversion_disk_write_ops[5m]))` |
+| `buildbuddy_remote_execution_image_fetch_duration_usec` | How long do tasks wait for the whole image fetch, including the outer per-image lock? | Histogram, isolation, registry, status, on_disk, has_creds, trigger, use_oci_fetcher | Existing | `histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(buildbuddy_remote_execution_image_fetch_duration_usec_bucket{isolation="firecracker"}[1h])))` |
+
+Validation covers bounded LRU history and active-flight tracking, end-to-end phase and IO sample counts across two real conversions, successful reconversion after filecache removal, failed conversions and disabled tracking, singleflight leaders/waiters/cancellation/distinct credentials, enabled process IO, sparse image apparent/allocated sizes, and once-only version reporting. The device-node conversion test skips cleanly without root and checks the resulting ext4 inode when run as root.
+
+Validation results:
+
+- Uncached non-root package run: ociconv (both test targets), ext4 metrics, and filecache passed; `//server/metrics:all` built with repository nogo checks. The root-only device-node case skipped. The existing ext4 `TestDirectoryToImageAutoSize_Reproducible` failed with its known image hash mismatch on e2fsprogs 1.47.0 (the reproducibility flag requires at least 1.47.2). This pre-existing failure is out of scope. [Invocation](https://app.buildbuddy.io/invocation/781a977d-ebf5-4a90-ab22-6066c1cff78b).
+- Uncached root run: all four targets (ociconv tests, ext4 metrics, and filecache) passed, including `TestRootConversionPhaseAccountingWithDeviceNode`, which executed and verified a character-device inode. Tests ran through a sudo wrapper with standalone execution; the wrapper restored output ownership so Bazel could collect results. [Invocation](https://app.buildbuddy.io/invocation/9819742e-792b-4bae-b4b5-c46bccb7be78).
+- The earlier Firecracker test attempt could not build its generated image prerequisites: `docker_enabled_x86_64_build` requires a root builder or `--config=remote`. Firecracker tests remain unverified. [Invocation](https://app.buildbuddy.io/invocation/d708cd9c-dc7d-4b26-a941-e29c7d6ed985).
+- All Bazel test runs used `--nocache_test_results`; compilation used the public CI cache with uploads disabled. `git diff --check` passed.
